# Migrations are hashed byte-for-byte.
#
# The migrator records sha256 of each applied file and refuses to continue if it
# ever changes (migrations/README.md explains why that rule is right). It hashes
# the raw bytes — so a file checked out as CRLF on Windows and as LF on Linux is
# *two different migrations* as far as that check is concerned, and a database
# migrated from CI can never be migrated again from a Windows workstation.
#
# Pinning the line endings costs nothing and removes the whole class.
migrations/*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reasoning, one step removed: these are copied into the runner image and
# executed there, and a stray CR is a syntax error in a shell script.
*.sh text eol=lf
